{"ts":"2026-07-26T11:30:20.670Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-07-26T11:30:20.670Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-07-26T11:30:20.669Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"GH-737 maps here (no new item). CodeFactor flagged 'Using a spread operator here creates a new array unnecessarily' at src/sdk/cli-contracts/flag-contracts.ts:113, commit 0d75347f.\n\nThe flagged construct is SUBCOMMAND_GLOBAL_FLAG_CONTRACTS, an array literal whose entire body is one spread of a mapped array:\n\n  export const SUBCOMMAND_GLOBAL_FLAG_CONTRACTS: CliFlagContract[] = [\n    ...RESERVED_EXTENSION_HOST_FLAGS.map((definition) => ({ ... })),\n  ];\n\nThe map already produces a new array; wrapping it in a literal copies it again. Reduces to dropping the brackets and the spread.\n\nMapped here rather than filed separately for two reasons. The file is this item's subject — the same per-command repetition this item exists to remove — so the restructuring will pass through this exact declaration. And the class already has an owner in the closed pm-zt1c (GH-553/GH-584, CodeFactor unnecessary-spread findings), so a fourth point item would fragment territory the registry already consolidated.\n\nWorth carrying into the fix: the two adjacent declarations show the same shape. GLOBAL_FLAG_CONTRACTS spreads SUBCOMMAND_GLOBAL_FLAG_CONTRACTS to append a single --version entry, which is legitimate, and the comment on GOVERNANCE_AND_CONTENT_FILTER_FLAG_CONTRACTS notes it is deliberately spread into two tables at a fixed position to preserve published contract order. Any dedupe must preserve that ordering guarantee — the published flag order is contract surface."}]}],"before_hash":"cb4c3e8434e9c7a937796b649bdeadde84d2f8c809ae287d5ed4e4876df1c66e","after_hash":"bb68a3e2479889db1e2a3f0fd9077b0d6d6a941fb59642341cb4c1b93b68569b"}
